Smart Pointers
When you need heap allocation beyond what Vec and String already handle, Rust provides smart pointer types. C++ developers will recognize the ideas.

Quick Reference
// Setup for examples below
use std::rc::Rc;
use std::sync::Arc;

let data = String::from("hello");










Type
Ownership
Thread-safe
C++ analogy
Example




